  id: venus
  title: Venus
  subtitle: EARTH'S SCORCHING TWIN
  paragraph: Almost Earth's twin in size, wrapped in thick carbon dioxide clouds that trap heat so effectively the surface sits near 465 degrees Celsius, hotter than Mercury. It turns backwards compared with most planets, and so slowly that its day outlasts its year.
